The highest GDPR fine tier is up to 20 000 000 EUR. For an undertaking, it is up to 4 % of total worldwide annual turnover of the preceding financial year, whichever is higher. [cite:B:gdpr-2016:438]

It applies to infringements of:
- the basic processing principles, including consent conditions (Articles 5, 6, 7 and 9);
- data subjects' rights (Articles 12 to 22);
- transfers to third countries or international organisations (Articles 44 to 49);
- obligations under Member State law adopted under Chapter IX;
- non-compliance with certain supervisory authority orders. [cite:B:gdpr-2016:438]

Non-compliance with an order under Article 58(2) falls in the same tier. [cite:B:gdpr-2016:439]

The lower tier is up to 10 000 000 EUR or 2 %. [cite:B:gdpr-2016:437]

Member States may decide whether and to what extent fines can be imposed on public authorities and bodies. [cite:B:gdpr-2016:439]

