Providers and deployers of AI systems must take measures to ensure, "to their best extent", a sufficient level of AI literacy. This covers their staff and other people who operate or use AI systems on their behalf. [cite:B:eu-ai-act-2024:323]

The measures must take into account:
- the technical knowledge, experience, education and training of those people;
- the context in which the AI systems will be used;
- the people or groups of people on whom the AI systems will be used. [cite:B:eu-ai-act-2024:323]

The recitals explain that AI literacy covers the following:
- applying the technical elements correctly during development;
- the measures to apply during use;
- interpreting the AI system's output. [cite:B:eu-ai-act-2024:38]

The recitals describe the duty as a way to give actors in the AI value chain the insights they need to comply with the Act. [cite:B:eu-ai-act-2024:39]

